"Encryption off. Backups are stored in plaintext and the live DB (if "
"encrypted) won't start. Default for anyone who has never configured "
"encryption. Change it as soon as you enable one of the other modes."


msgid ""
"Massima sicurezza contro furto del disco: la passphrase non viene mai "
"scritta su disco. Stoic la chiede a ogni avvio e la tiene solo in RAM. Se "
"Stoic non gira, niente decifra il DB. Implica: ogni 'make run' richiede una "
"digitazione; i backup notturni richiedono Stoic acceso."
msgstr ""
"Maximum security against disk theft: the passphrase is never written to "
"disk. Stoic asks for it at every startup and keeps it in RAM only. If Stoic "
"isn't running, nothing can decrypt the DB. Implies: every 'make run' "
"requires typing it; nightly backups need Stoic running."


msgid ""
"Comodità massima: la passphrase è in instance/backup.key (permessi 0600). "
"Stoic la legge automaticamente al boot. Backup notturni funzionano anche se "
"Stoic non è in uso. Vulnerabile se l'attaccante prende disco + file di "
"chiave."
msgstr ""
"Maximum convenience: the passphrase lives in instance/backup.key (0600 "
"permissions). Stoic reads it automatically at boot. Nightly backups work "
"even when Stoic isn't in use. Vulnerable if an attacker gets the disk + the "
"key file."


msgid ""
"Adatta a deployment server (systemd-creds, Docker secrets, ecc): la "
"passphrase è iniettata via env var prima del lancio. Equivalente in "
"sicurezza al modo 'file' nella maggior parte dei casi d'uso desktop."
msgstr ""
"Suited to server deployments (systemd-creds, Docker secrets, etc.): the "
"passphrase is injected via env var before launch. Security-equivalent to the"
" 'file' mode in most desktop use cases."


